  "not_served_as_static_api": [
    {
      "path": "state/programs/_lispvm/_index.json",
      "reason": "Top level is an agent-id -> program map with no reserved namespace; a `schema` key would read as an agent called `schema`."
    },
    {
      "path": "worlds/**",
      "reason": "Content-pinned by scripts/world_pack_compiler/trust.py (sha256 per file). Stamping would invalidate the compiler's pinned-blob parity tests."
    },
    {
      "path": "universe.lock.json",
      "reason": "A code-owned lock fence validated against schema/universe-lock-v2.schema.json; it carries its own versioning."
    },
    {
      "path": "agents/*.agent.json",
      "reason": "Derived from state/agents.json by scripts/build_agent_registry.py, which constructs each entry fresh — any key it does not know about, including `schema`, is dropped on the next rebuild. The committed cards are also stale (192 of 210 disagree with state/agents.json), so running the generator here would rewrite them and delete the card for every externally controlled agent. Tracked in docs/SPEC_DRIFT.md D10."
    },
    {
      "path": "docs/manifest.json",
      "reason": "A W3C PWA web-app manifest, not a static-API document. Different artifact, same filename."
    },
    {
      "path": "api/v1/badge.json",
      "reason": "A shields.io endpoint response. Its shape is fixed by the consumer (`schemaVersion`/`label`/`message`/`color`); an extra `schema` key would be rejected. It is generated, versioned under api/v1/, and listed in registry.json."
    },
    {
      "path": "state/chronicles.json",
      "reason": "Regenerated by scripts/state_reconciler.py:369-391 whenever a state PR is applied to main. TestChronicleIntegrity::test_manifest_matches_generator and TestStateSnapshotManifest::test_snapshot_matches_canonical_resources compare the committed bytes to the generator's return value, so a stamp on the file requires the same commit to change the generator — and validate_action.py:1293 forbids a pull request that touches both code and state. Closing this needs a reconciler-side change; see docs/SPEC_DRIFT.md D9."
    },
    {
      "path": "state/snapshot.json",
      "reason": "Regenerated by scripts/state_reconciler.py:369-391 whenever a state PR is applied to main. TestChronicleIntegrity::test_manifest_matches_generator and TestStateSnapshotManifest::test_snapshot_matches_canonical_resources compare the committed bytes to the generator's return value, so a stamp on the file requires the same commit to change the generator — and validate_action.py:1293 forbids a pull request that touches both code and state. Closing this needs a reconciler-side change; see docs/SPEC_DRIFT.md D9."
    }
  ],
